{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 4, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 17447932663297596016, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 637, "mtime": 1791871703.6100435, "sha256": "752685b302f702a4a703fe738f5cb1f471931f52998ee379c5e3b87f5c5aa441"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 472, "mtime": 1791871707.034252, "sha256": "63053ce001dd4bcf0b8a223ed4a58549139133a6a771b53a316006deca5061f5"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/transcripts/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/2/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-38/omp-38/cells/without/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/2/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/27517f255bc0f6927f6358a38d2c34b2efe166af/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Now a regression test, plus a run of the suite.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** there were two problems. Python stores `2.675` as `2.67499999\u2026`, and the built-in `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (so `round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`). The docstring says \"half up\", but the code never did that.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the value into a `Decimal` using `repr(x)`, which gives `\"2.675\"`, then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a float, so nothing that calls it needs to change. Negative values round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`).\n\n**Verification:** pytest isn't installed here, so I didn't run any test files, including the new `tests/test_round_money.py`. I checked by calling the functions directly instead:\n- `round_money` gives `2.68, 0.13, 1.01, 2.67, 2.0, -2.68` for `2.675, 0.125, 1.005, 2.674, 2.0, -2.675`.\n- `add_vat(10)` gives `12.0` and `split(10.00, 3)` gives `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`, as before.\n\n**Still wrong, not fixed:** `add_vat` multiplies in floats before it rounds. `2.2375 * 1.2` should be exactly `2.685`, but in floats it comes out as `2.6849999999999996`, so `add_vat(2.2375)` returns `2.68` instead of `2.69`. Doing the multiplication in `Decimal` inside `add_vat` would fix this. I left it alone because you only asked about `round_money`; say if you want it.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 248566, "requests_cache_write": 11153, "requests_cost_usd": 0.16155819999999999, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2800, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "run_seed":